The Scala class regex doesn't match private class ... because private is not in the alternation (?:abstract|sealed|final|implicit|lazy). So `private class PrivateClass` won't be captured at all. The Scala visibility check in extract_scala_symbols is:

```rust
let is_pub = !trimmed.starts_with("private") && !trimmed.starts_with("protected");
```

But the regex for class doesn't match private class at all, so the symbol isn't even extracted. Same for protected def — the RE_SCALA_DEF regex does include private|protected in its modifier list, so that one should match. Let me verify:

The Scala class regex includes abstract|sealed|final|implicit|lazy but NOT private|protected. So private class PrivateClass won't match the class regex at all. But `private def privateDef() will match because RE_SCALA_DEF includes private|protected`.

